  body: "# Category A contribution conditions: dated scope\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe captured Category
    A guidance separates the single-contribution-condition route for people reaching pensionable age from 6 April
    2010 to before 6 April 2016 from the earlier contribution conditions retained in an appendix.\n\n## Scope and
    exceptions\n\nThe quoted year count is not a universal State Pension rule. Claims, qualifying earnings factors,
    credits, reduced rates, record disputes and the claimant’s actual pensionable-age date require review; no entitlement
    is calculated.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 75026, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=9).\n\
    - [DMG 75027, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=9).\n\
    - [DMG 75030, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=10).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch75` — PDF SHA-256 `655e7acb31f09f5169efbe40419091ee479f88c0c45b65c7a507b042b67712f9`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `0d037880d2aeaff1be89235ee987ca4acb1c839fcf1ead8b8be2daa9f6795465`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/rp-contribution-record-dispute
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter routes disputes about the Category A contribution record to HMRC instead of
      treating the obtained record as incontestable.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch75/0010
      quote: "75032 Entitlement to Cat A RP depends on the contribution conditions being satisfied. In practice
        the NI\ncontribution record is usually obtained and any decision is based on the assumption that the record
        is\nfactually correct. However, where there is a dispute about the record, the matter must be referred by
        the\n\nDM to HMRC for a formal decision1. That referral should be made2 to:\nHMRC\nNational Insurance Contributions
        Office\nNE98 1ZZ\n\n\nNote 1: See DMG Chapters 03, 04 and 06 for guidance on how decisions and appeals are
        handled after a\nreference to HMRC.\n\n\nNote 2: See DMG Chapter 01 where the dispute is about whether credits
        should be awarded.\n\n\n     1 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 11A and 38A; 2 Secretary of State for Work and Pensions
        v TB v HMRC (RP)\n                                                                                     \
        \                    [2010]\n                                                                          \
        \   UKUT 88 (AAC) [2010] AACR 38"
      locator: DMG 75032
